  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{7}{3x}?$",
  "worked_solution": "To plot $y=-\\frac{7}{3x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{7}{3}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{7}{3x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/ed5613c7614ab24b823ba0729ed1a19e2d0e57a4b81c0ba7868ccb61a52e7904.png)",
